>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:59:47-07:00","id":952691,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for an established sorcerer using a Contract to help in his night-job as a burglar or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:20:35-07:00","id":952780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=952610#post952610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These are less than Fae Touched. Fae-Touched have Glamour, and can make Pledges, etc. Literally the only thing a Hedge Sorcerer has is Contracts. They don't even have the Glamor for them (usually), so they <i>need</i> to use the Catches.</div> </div> </div> </div> Understood, you intend to make the Hedge Sorceror a lesser, lesser Temlmplae, were as Fae Touched are more medium template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:52:13-07:00","id":952797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=952686#post952686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the intro fiction, I might have a go tomorrow. Would about 1k words be enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I only seem to be able to envision things in disjointed pieces. Nothing suitable for actual view.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=952689#post952689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do you want an established sorcerer, one only making his first bargain, a group of hunters dealing with what they think is a mortal, only for him to pull out the Contracts...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever you feel would drive home the flavor. Just remember that they need to invoke the Catches to actually use their Contracts. Maybe something that demonstrates the foresight required, or something that demonstrates what happens when you <i>can't</i> fulfill the Catch triggers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-17-2016, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T15:56:21-07:00","id":952802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=952780#post952780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Understood, you intend to make the Hedge Sorceror a lesser, lesser Temlmplae, were as Fae Touched are more medium template.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. As absolutely bare-bones as necessary to use Contracts. Thankfully, Contracts are already priced as Merits, and have a mechanism to activate (the Catch) without needing to muck around with fuel or conversions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T08:43:18-07:00","id":975072,"title":"","content":"Your Hedge Sorceror may want to have a look at the rules for the Hedge, you might want to make some additions to your Hedge Sorceror or take it in a different direction. Either way it seems like they'd qualify for Master Shaper merit and maybe the Hollow Merit too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T09:25:29-07:00","id":975093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=975072#post975072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Hedge Sorceror may want to have a look at the rules for the Hedge, you might want to make some additions to your Hedge Sorceror or take it in a different direction. Either way it seems like they'd qualify for Master Shaper merit and maybe the Hollow Merit too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to take a look later. Though, as stated, Hedge Sorcerers might not ever actually see the Hedge itself. (The term &quot;Hedge Sorcerer&quot; is derived from them being &quot;low magic&quot; users, and the fact that the specific magic they use is Changeling Contracts)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T10:32:26-07:00","id":975114,"title":"","content":"In the playtest, it has been established Goblin Contracts are literal bargains with powerful Hobs who demand a literal part of their &quot;clients&quot; in exchange for their powers. I would wait to see more about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T10:47:15-07:00","id":975123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=975093#post975093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll try to take a look later. Though, as stated, Hedge Sorcerers might not ever actually see the Hedge itself. (The term &amp;quot;Hedge Sorcerer&amp;quot; is derived from them being &amp;quot;low magic&amp;quot; users, and the fact that the specific magic they use is Changeling Contracts)</div> </div> </div> </div> That does make sense. You Hedge Sorceror reminds me of the D&amp;D Feylock fluff wise, but with a Changeling twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:48:55-07:00","id":976129,"title":"","content":"What about a merit which allows the character to draw glamour from a Goblin or Fae, at the cost of a &quot;favor&quot; or service for each X points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T04:19:36-07:00","id":976460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=976129#post976129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a merit which allows the character to draw glamour from a Goblin or Fae, at the cost of a &quot;favor&quot; or service for each X points?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could. How to package and represent that mechanically, though? I suppose gaining an &quot;indebted&quot; Condition scaled or for each glamour might work. The Pact system can do this anyways, though.<br /> <br /> And besides - being starved for Glamour is part of the fun. Needing an animal nearby for Fang and Talon, or tricking a foe into challenging you to a game for Know the Competition adds to the strange flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:38:08-07:00","id":976496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=976460#post976460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Could. How to package and represent that mechanically, though? I suppose gaining an &quot;indebted&quot; Condition scaled or for each glamour might work. The Pact system can do this anyways, though.<br /> <br /> And besides - being starved for Glamour is part of the fun. Needing an animal nearby for Fang and Talon, or tricking a foe into challenging you to a game for Know the Competition adds to the strange flavor.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Still, the possibility of avoiding racking your brains with the damn catches<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, all </span></span></span>in exchange for, every full moon, sending some random girl to the closed lake where &quot;allegedly&quot; a Vodianoi has his home, may be a bit tempting to ignore for some sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:53:54-07:00","id":976500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=976496#post976496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Still, the possibility of avoiding racking your brains with the damn catches<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, all </span></span></span>in exchange for, every full moon, sending some random girl to the closed lake where &quot;allegedly&quot; a Vodianoi has his home, may be a bit tempting to ignore for some sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely. The limitations imposed by Catches are a major limiter on Hedge Sorcerers. One who can break those restrictions is a big game-changer, relatively speaking. And the temptation to do so, likely drives a number to dark places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:46:42-07:00","id":977785,"title":"","content":"A Condition that may see some use, for Hedge Sorcerers or Changelings (if desired). Possible sources are broken promises, false words, or anything that could give one the Oath-Breaker Condition. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Forsworn (Persistent)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Wyrd looks unkindly upon those who break their sworn oaths, turning from them and giving their claims to power less credence. The Character suffers a penalty on Contract activation equal to their Wyrd (minimum 1). If their base dice pool for a Contract is ever reduced to -5, then activation of the Contract becomes impossible. This Condition can be gained multiple times for different infractions, and the penalties stack.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Swearing upon the Wyrd or one's power. Violating a Pledge. Disobeying a behavioral Frailty.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Beat:</b> Succeed on a Contract activation roll that has been reduced to a Chance Die due to this Condition.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Resolution:</b> Making restitution for your broken oath to the injured party, or an acceptable (to the Wyrd) representative. A decent benchmark would be if it would be equivalent to fulfilling a long-term Aspiration, or qualify for a full Willpower refresh.</span></span> <hr /><br /> Hedge Sorcerers will only be affected by this at -1 per instance (usually; those who've boosted their power with Supernatural Potency will find their power turns against them <i>quicker</i>), but with their lower Dice Pools, those penalties add up. Changelings will find one instance robbing them of using Wyrd in their Contract <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pools, but additional instances penalizing them further. High Wyrd Changelings (or Hedge Sorcerers) better be extremely careful before a few broken Oaths steal much of their power.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-28-2016, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T17:53:02-08:00","id":1177467,"title":"","content":"Update:<br /> <br /> So far, I'm thinking Hedge Sorcerers can pick up Common Arcadian (and Court, provided they get Court Goodwill somehow) Contracts as a 3-dot Merit (since nothing is favored, the XP cost is 3 for Common). I'm debating on having them pick up a minor Frailty per Contract, though. They still have no Glamour pool, and so must use the Loopholes. There might be rumors of them acquiring Royal Contracts (Drawback: Major Frailty per?). <br /> <br /> Goblin Contracts are fair game, of course, with all the risks those entail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T12:36:53-08:00","id":1177659,"title":"","content":"By making it a merit template a Changeling can use a dream assailant condition via dream weaving to make a mortal a hedge sorcerer. Just an interesting twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T07:28:42-08:00","id":1178069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=1177659#post1177659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By making it a merit template a Changeling can use a dream assailant condition via dream weaving to make a mortal a hedge sorcerer. Just an interesting twist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting and appropriate, I think.<br /> <br /> I like the minor template. It reminds me of stories where (especially peasant) children discover a kind of fae charm that actually works--for them. Usually things do not go well.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T08:54:01-08:00","id":1178086,"title":"","content":"Here is the latest update for version 2.0, to keep with the rules changes in Changeling 2E:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wyrd Bargain (Supernatural, \u2022\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You\u2019ve struck a bargain with Hobgoblins, Fae, or the Wyrd itself (even if you don\u2019t realize it, or know it by that name at the time). You have signed into a Contact and can invoke it as if you were a Changeling (see below). This doesn\u2019t give you a Wyrd score to contribute to rolls (assume you only have a Wyrd of 1, when an effect is calculated by Wyrd alone), nor does it give you a Glamour pool, necessitating you to use the Loopholes of individual Contracts. You acquire a Goblin Contract at two dots, a Common Arcadian or Court Contract at three dots, or a Royal Arcadian or Court Contract at four dots. You must still meet any prerequisites, such as minimum Court Goodwill for Court Contracts.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Your deal with the Wyrd has certain stipulations. For Common Contracts, you take on a Minor Frailty, thematic with your particular deal, representing how you uphold your end of the bargain, or a curse incurred for access to such powers. For Royal Contacts, it is instead a Major Frailty. Goblin Contracts incur no Frailty... but Goblin Debt is still a factor.<br /> <b>Special:</b> This merit can be acquired multiple times, each time representing another Contract. The Frailties stack with each acquisition.</span></span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Sidebar: Hedge Sorcerers as Goblins?</b><br /> Despite a strong trade in Goblin Contracts, the &quot;average&quot; Hedge Sorcerer rarely accrues enough Goblin Debt to gain the Hedge Denizen Condition. Whatever forces empower such contracts seems to prefer calling in their due before it accumulates that high. In most cases. Storytellers can optionally use the following system: Maximum Goblin Debt is 11 - current Integrity, with some consequence applying before a Hedge Sorcerer would acquire any more (even if it means penalizing the activation roll of a Goblin Contract that would put the Sorcerer over their &quot;limit&quot;). This means Hedge Sorcerers with a steady worldview (high Integrity) have little to fear from Conditions (if not &quot;random&quot; penalties) imposed by Goblin Debt, while the most far gone (Integrity 1) <i>do</i> risk becoming something other than human by their bargains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-22-2018, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T11:06:10-08:00","id":1178111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers?p=1178086#post1178086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the latest update for version 2.0, to keep with the rules changes in Changeling 2E:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wyrd Bargain (Supernatural, \u2022\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You\u2019ve struck a bargain with Hobgoblins, Fae, or the Wyrd itself (even if you don\u2019t realize it, or know it by that name at the time). You have signed into a Contact and can invoke it as if you were a Changeling (see below). This doesn\u2019t give you a Wyrd score to contribute to rolls (assume you only have a Wyrd of 1, when an effect is calculated by Wyrd alone), nor does it give you a Glamour pool, necessitating you to use the Loopholes of individual Contracts. You acquire a Goblin Contract at two dots, a Common Arcadian or Court Contract at three dots, or a Royal Arcadian or Court Contract at four dots. You must still meet any prerequisites, such as minimum Court Goodwill for Court Contracts.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Your deal with the Wyrd has certain stipulations. For Common Contracts, you take on a Minor Frailty, thematic with your particular deal, representing how you uphold your end of the bargain, or a curse incurred for access to such powers. For Royal Contacts, it is instead a Major Frailty. Goblin Contracts incur no Frailty... but Goblin Debt is still a factor.<br /> <b>Special:</b> This merit can be acquired multiple times, each time representing another Contract. The Frailties stack with each acquisition.</span></span> <hr /><br /> <b>Sidebar: Hedge Sorcerers as Goblins?</b><br /> Despite a strong trade in Goblin Contracts, the &quot;average&quot; Hedge Sorcerer rarely accrues enough Goblin Debt to gain the Hedge Denizen Condition. Whatever forces empower such contracts seems to prefer calling in their due before it accumulates that high. In most cases. Storytellers can optionally use the following system: Maximum Goblin Debt is 11 - current Integrity, with some consequence applying before a Hedge Sorcerer would acquire any more (even if it means penalizing the activation roll of a Goblin Contract that would put the Sorcerer over their &quot;limit&quot;). This means Hedge Sorcerers with a steady worldview (high Integrity) have little to fear from Conditions (if not &quot;random&quot; penalties) imposed by Goblin Debt, while the most far gone (Integrity 1) <i>do</i> risk becoming something other than human by their bargains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, this pretty much fits a certain fan Conspiracy\u00b4s endowment: <a href=\"https://vindae.tumblr.com/post/97325142360/sugar-spice-and-magically-binding-contracts\" target=\"_blank\">https://vindae.tumblr.com/post/97325...ding-contracts</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T15:31:36-08:00","id":1178233,"title":"","content":"As an alterative or addition to the above, what about a character who has learned &quot;recipes&quot;, in which they collect fruits and hedge detris, throw them in a pot, and create a heady brew of fae magic that has certain magical effects (if done correctly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"h